# ==============================================================================
# GhostKey Tor Onion Service Configuration (v3 Hidden Service)
# ==============================================================================
# Run with: tor -f torrc
#
# Once Tor starts, it will generate a '.onion' hostname inside:
# ./hidden_service/hostname
#
# Give that .onion address to the app!
# The ISP and outside world will only see encrypted Tor traffic to Guard nodes.
# ==============================================================================

DataDirectory ./tor_data

# Tor v3 Onion Service
HiddenServiceDir ./hidden_service/
HiddenServiceVersion 3
HiddenServicePort 80 127.0.0.1:8765

# Security Hardening
AvoidDiskWrites 1
SafeLogging 1
Log notice stdout

# This Tor instance only hosts the onion service; it does not need to expose a
# local SOCKS proxy. (Clients use their own Tor/Orbot.) Re-enable only if you
# deliberately want a SOCKS listener on this machine.
# SocksPort 9050
